TITLE:: PianoRollContainer
SUMMARY:: Tabbed container that directs keystrokes and recording MIDI to one piano roll.
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events
RELATED:: Classes/MIDIdef, Classes/PianoRoll, Classes/PianoRollPattern, Classes/Sequencer, Classes/SequencerDocument, Classes/SequencerGui, Classes/SequencerKeyRouter, Classes/Tabset

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::PianoRollContainer:: is a LINK::Classes/SCViewHolder:: whose view is a LINK::Classes/Tabset:: of LINK::Classes/PianoRoll::s. The first roll is created by calling the tabset's LINK::Classes/Tabset#-addViewFunc::, and the CODE::+:: tab uses that same function. Every roll created that way is named Sequence plus an incrementing count, starting at 1. LINK::#-openPattern:: adds a tab under a caller-supplied name, loads a LINK::Classes/PianoRollPattern:: into a fresh roll, and selects that tab. It posts a warning and returns false while the selected roll is recording. The container registers the record-context actions CODE::\assignPart1:: through CODE::\assignPart9::, CODE::\delete::, CODE::\focusCommandPrompt::, CODE::\redo::, CODE::\redoY::, and CODE::\undo:: once on the shared LINK::Classes/SequencerKeyRouter::, and those actions call the selected roll. It subscribes to that roll. When the roll announces CODE::\isRecording:: as CODE::true::, the container sets the tabset's LINK::Classes/Tabset#-canSwitchTab:: to CODE::false::, so neither another tab nor CODE::+:: can be selected until recording stops. Unless dev mode is on, it also installs CODE::recordMidi_noteOn:: and CODE::recordMidi_noteOff:: and forwards each message to LINK::Classes/PianoRoll#-receiveRecordingMidi::. When recording stops, it frees those defs and allows tab switching again. Loops that are already playing are left running. LINK::#-stopAll:: stops the loop and recording on every roll.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a TELETYPE::PianoRollContainer:: with one piano roll already selected. That roll is produced by the tabset's LINK::Classes/Tabset#-addViewFunc::, so its name is Sequence 1.

ARGUMENT:: palette
The LINK::Classes/GuiPalette:: passed to every LINK::Classes/PianoRoll::.

ARGUMENT:: sequencer
The LINK::Classes/Sequencer:: passed to every LINK::Classes/PianoRoll::.

ARGUMENT:: devMode
When CODE::true::, recording does not install MIDI input. The default is CODE::false::.

ARGUMENT:: keyRouter
The LINK::Classes/SequencerKeyRouter:: whose record-context actions this container registers.

ARGUMENT:: sequencerDocument
The optional LINK::Classes/SequencerDocument:: passed to every LINK::Classes/PianoRoll::. CODE::nil:: is allowed.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::PianoRollContainer:: instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: openPattern
Adds a tab named CODE::name::, loads CODE::pattern:: into a fresh roll, and selects that tab. CODE::midiChannel:: is passed to that roll. Returns false, and posts a warning, when the selected roll is recording.

ARGUMENT:: name
A LINK::Classes/String:: used as the tab title.

ARGUMENT:: pattern
A LINK::Classes/PianoRollPattern::.

ARGUMENT:: midiChannel
A LINK::Classes/SimpleNumber::, or CODE::nil::. Passed to LINK::Classes/PianoRoll#-loadPattern::.

RETURNS::
CODE::true:: when the tab was added, CODE::false:: when recording blocked it.

METHOD:: stopAll
Stops the loop and recording on every LINK::Classes/PianoRoll:: in the tabset, and frees any recording LINK::Classes/MIDIdef::s this container installed.

METHOD:: update
Receives LINK::Classes/PianoRoll:: notifications. CODE::\isRecording:: with CODE::true:: blocks tab switching and, unless dev mode is on, installs the recording LINK::Classes/MIDIdef::s. CODE::false:: frees those defs and allows tab switching again.

ARGUMENT:: theChanged
The LINK::Classes/PianoRoll:: that changed.

ARGUMENT:: what
The notification symbol. CODE::\isRecording:: is handled.

ARGUMENT:: isRecording
CODE::true:: when that roll has started recording, CODE::false:: when it has stopped.

PRIVATE:: init, prAddRoll, prAssignPart, prDeleteSelected, prFocusCommandPrompt, prFreeRecordingMidi, prInstallRecordingMidi, prMakeRoll, prRedo, prRegisterKeyHandlers, prSelectRoll, prUndo
